<title>MEXICO: Mexico Jan coffee exports outstrip Jan '96 total.</title>
<headline>Mexico Jan coffee exports outstrip Jan '96 total.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican coffee exports in January outstripped the same month a year earlier by 17.5 percent or 130,476 60-kg bags, the Mexican Coffee Council said in a report obtained Tuesday.</p>
<p>The council, Mexico's umbrella organisation for the whole sector, said exports in the month were 875,904 60-kg bags compared to the 745,428 bags in January 1996.  </p>
<p>In the first four months of the October-September 1996-1997 cycle (October through January), Mexico has exported 1,750,379 bags compared to 1,565,295 bags in the same four month period, up 185,084 bags, or an 11.8 percent hike.</p>
<p>No reasons were given for the increase in exports over 1995-1996, which itself was a record export year for Mexican producers and traders.</p>
<p>A full breakdown of the Mexican exports follows in table form. Figures are for 60-kg bags.</p>
<p>    Month     1996-1997	 1995-1996	    1994-1995</p>
<p>    October    163,489	   101,912		 59,303</p>
<p>    November   320,843	   296,510		131,767</p>
<p>    December   390,143	   421,445		260,081</p>
<p>    January    875,904	   745,428		586,669</p>
<p>    February			 744,586		460,060</p>
<p>    March			    633,648		603,537</p>
<p>    April			    528,944		243,772</p>
<p>    May				456,768		287,238</p>
<p>    June			     193,627		217,951</p>
<p>    July			     219,432		121,033</p>
<p>    August			   146,745		184,466</p>
<p>    September			 86,982		101,867</p>
